  "problem": "The third-order differential equation ${y}^{\u2034}-4{y}^{\u2033}+{t}^{2}{y}^{\u2032}+{e}^{t}y=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t$ can be expressed as the matrix equation ${x}^{\u2032}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t),$ where\n\n| $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,A=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  | $\\,,\\,f(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-4}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} | {{field-7}} |  |  | {{field-8}} |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-9}} | {{field-10}} | {{field-11}} |  |  | {{field-12}} |  |  |  |\n\nand for $y=y(t),$ we have $y={x}_{1}(t),$ ${y}^{\u2032}={x}_{2}(t),$ and ${y}^{\u2033}={x}_{3}(t).$",
